#: ../../source/performance-now_README.md:3
msgid ""
"Implements a function similar to `performance.now` (based on "
"`process.hrtime`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/performance-now_README.md:5
msgid ""
"Modern browsers have a `window.performance` object with - among others - "
"a `now` method which gives time in milliseconds, but with sub-millisecond"
" precision. This module offers the same function based on the Node.js "
"native `process.hrtime` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/performance-now_README.md:7
msgid ""
"Using `process.hrtime` means that the reported time will be monotonically"
" increasing, and not subject to clock-drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/performance-now_README.md:9
msgid ""
"According to the [High Resolution Time "
"specification](http://www.w3.org/TR/hr-time/), the number of milliseconds"
" reported by `performance.now` should be relative to the value of "
"`performance.timing.navigationStart`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/performance-now_README.md:11
msgid ""
"In the current version of the module (2.0) the reported time is relative "
"to the time the current Node process has started (inferred from "
"`process.uptime()`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/performance-now_README.md:13
msgid ""
"Version 1.0 reported a different time. The reported time was relative to "
"the time the module was loaded (i.e. the time it was first `require`d). "
"If you need this functionality, version 1.0 is still available on NPM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/performance-now_README.md:15
msgid "Example usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/performance-now_README.md:25
msgid ""
"Running the now function two times right after each other yields a time "
"difference of a few microseconds. Given this overhead, I think it's best "
"to assume that the precision of intervals computed with this method is "
"not higher than 10 microseconds, if you don't know the exact overhead on "
"your own system."
msgstr ""

